# NG-RT-REFRACTION-NIGHT: the night half of NG-RT-REFRACTION.scn (designs F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3C-DESIGN.md and
# F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3-DESIGN.md, «## Приёмка»; physics F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION2-DESIGN.md). One editor
# session in F:/BistroFoliageProj, GI_Bistro_Night: the shop window as path tracer | Translucency.Refraction
# ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced | HardwareTraced with the composite off | with one interface bend - one camera, one
# exposure, one time, one tier.
# The path tracer is the reference: GlobalIllumination + Reflections PathTraced (the tracer pairs them). The raster
# frames keep Reflections / GI HardwareTraced; only the Translucency rows change between night_ss, night_rt and
# night_rt_mute.
# The tier (D7): every group of the preset is pinned at High before any row (a group level drops that group's rows,
# so the pins come first); the benchmark preset chooses nothing in this run. Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer is
# not set here (High = 1): the night isolates the refraction; the day proves D1. An unattended run keeps every
# Quality change in this process (QualityState::KeepInSession): machine.json is never written; the tail still
# clears the rows. There is no group "Level" command: the next run starts from the machine's own selection.
# A/B order (D8, D9; 3C): night_ss -> night_rt -> night_ss_b -> night_rt_mute -> night_rt_b -> night_rt_mi1 with
# the camera still, 256 frames each,
# and only then the two 16-frame turns (D10); night_ss vs night_ss_b (ScreenSpace twice, night_rt between them) is
# the drift of the scenario itself, the bound for every opaque-pixel comparison.
# night_rt_mute: HardwareTraced with Translucency.RefractionComposite 0 (the glass cell ignores the trace): its
# opaque pixels vs night_ss show whether the pass's graph reads move them (D9).
# The knockout of [night_rt] (3C D1): night_rt_b is HardwareTraced again after night_rt_mute, the camera still
# (the run noise); |night_rt - night_rt_mute| >= 2 x |night_rt - night_rt_b|, mean |delta| of (R+G+B)/3 (0..255)
# over the pane mask = rectangle x540-1260 y170-630, pixels where night_pt > 8 (KO3C-NIGHT: 5.42 against 7.43 -
# the trace's answer never reached the frame once the interface budget ran out). night_rt_mi1 is HardwareTraced
# with Translucency.RefractionMaxInterfaces 1: the budget bounds the bends, not the answer, so the glass differs
# from night_rt_mute at least as much as night_rt does.
# The window rule (D6): a GPU time is a budget number only when the window is free - in BOTH dumps of a pair (ss
# and rt) "ClearMainFramebuffer" <= 0.2 ms, and their "GPU frame" differ by less than 2x; else the number is not
# a measurement and the run is repeated. Budget at 1080p = ms x 2073600 / (viewport width x height), the
# viewport size from editor.log (1787x657 today = 1.17 Mpx). Every measured capture has its own profile-dump
# (reply line_NNN_profile-dump.txt) right before it.
# Frame wait: `frames N` (N presented frames). Every compared capture stands >= 256 frames after the last
# GlobalIllumination.Method switch or camera turn (GI accumulation converged; else the opaque pixels drift).
# The camera faces the cafe shop window Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_bottom_4711
# (MASTER_Glass_Exterior, StaticMeshGlass; pane pivot -108,197,-719, centre ~y 320) from 3 m out on the terrace.
# One exposure: AutoExposure off (at the scene's own ManualExposureEV100), back on in the tail.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/GI_Bistro_Night.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Textures High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Filtering High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shadows High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Reflections High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PostProcess High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Effects High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: AntiAliasing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ResolutionScale High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shading High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PathTracing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Foliage High"
Дано run Anti-Aliasing "Anti-Aliasing: TAA"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Resolution.Percent 100"
# The profile-dumps carry GPU times only with GPU profiling on (Profiler "GPU"; off, every scope reads gpu 0.000).
Дано run Debug "GPU profiling: On"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -370,300,-861
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.8806,0.07,0.4738
Дано set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.AutoExposure false
# --- night: path tracer | ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced | HardwareTraced, composite off - the camera does not move
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method PathTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method PathTraced"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид night_pt night, path tracer: the reference - the interior lamps behind the glass, the second glass / bottles behind the window
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда-вид night_ss night, ScreenSpace: the A side of every comparison - mean L of the glass area vs night_pt recorded; profile-dump: the window rule (ClearMainFramebuffer <= 0.2 ms)
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction HardwareTraced"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда refr_pass "Translucency: Ray Traced Refraction" in the night_rt dump: GPU time non-zero and <= 1.0 ms scaled to 1080p (ms x 2073600 / viewport width x height); the window holds by the rule (ClearMainFramebuffer <= 0.2 ms in the night_ss and night_rt dumps, their GPU frame within 2x)
Тогда-вид night_rt night, HardwareTraced: differs from night_ss only inside the glass pixels; the opaque-pixel difference to night_ss is not above the night_ss / night_ss_b pair; the interior lamps behind the glass in place, the second glass / bottles behind the window visible; night_rt vs night_rt_mute on the glass at least 2x night_rt vs night_rt_b (mean |delta| over the pane mask, see the head)
# The drift bound, interleaved as KO-NIGHT (ss -> rt -> ss, camera still, 256 frames each): night_ss_b is ScreenSpace
# again 256 frames after night_rt; night_ss vs night_ss_b is the ss-ss drift of this run (HW GI temporal noise).
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид night_ss_b night, ScreenSpace again 256 frames after night_rt, the camera still: night_ss vs night_ss_b (mean abs over the opaque pixels) is the ss-ss drift measured in this run - the bound [night_rt] and night_rt_mute are held to
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite 0"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда-вид night_rt_mute night, HardwareTraced, composite off (Translucency.RefractionComposite 0): the opaque pixels match night_ss within the night_ss / night_ss_b drift; if not, the cause of D9 is the pass's reads in the graph and the feature goes back to the architect with this frame; profile-dump vs night_rt: the composite's share (D11)
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite Level"
# --- the knockout of night_rt (3C D1): HardwareTraced again (the run noise), then the interface budget at 1
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид night_rt_b night, HardwareTraced again after night_rt_mute, the camera still: night_rt vs night_rt_b (mean |delta| over the pane mask) is the run noise [night_rt] is held to
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionMaxInterfaces 1"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид night_rt_mi1 night, HardwareTraced, Translucency.RefractionMaxInterfaces 1: the glass differs from night_rt_mute not less than night_rt does (mean |delta| over the pane mask) - the trace answers whatever the interface budget
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionMaxInterfaces Level"
